 "text": "For 40 years, U.S. government doctors watched hundreds of Black men with syphilis and didn't treat them. It was the Tuskegee study, starting in 1932 in Alabama. The men were told they had bad blood. By the 1940s, penicillin was the cure. They still didn't get it. Here's the trick. Free meals, free rides, free burial insurance. Kindness kept them coming back. In 1972, a whistleblower went to the press. The study ended that year. Follow for more dark psychology.",
